## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design practical CAPA governance tied to real-time data flows and multi-tenant risk without overengineering.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model fields (id, tenant_ids, sink, data_classification, evidence, region, remediation_links, state)
- Region-aware lifecycle states
- Minimal REST API (POST /caps, PATCH /caps/{id})
- Metrics: recurrence_rate, MTTR, false_positives, containment_time per region
- RCA template and safe-canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express endpoints for CAPA creation
const app = require('express')();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => { /* create CAPA */ res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' }); });
app.patch('/caps/:id', (req, res) => { /* update CAPA */ res.status(200).send({ ok: true }); });
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for privacy-policy drift in a multi-tenant, partner‑integrated data plane. Requires data modeling, lifecycle management, API surfaces, observability, and rollout safety.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model including lineage and policy versions
- Region/tenant-aware metrics
- Lifecycle state machine and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback safeguards

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  rootCause?: string;
  correctiveAction?: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'investigating'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  timestamps: { detected: string; updated?: string; closed?: string };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollout for a policy upgrade in this scenario?
- What data access controls and retention would you enforce during CAPA investigations?
